# Security Rules

Read: `docs/security/security-policy.md`, `docs/security/hmac.md`, `docs/security/token-system.md`

## Always

- Store secrets in env / Android Keystore / `SecurePreferences` — never commit `.env`, private keys, or live API secrets.
- JWT for session auth; verify expiry and role claims server-side.
- HMAC for SMS / device integrity paths — preserve replay protection and timestamp/nonce checks where implemented.
- Parameterized queries via Prisma only — no string-concat SQL.
- Sanitize/validate all external input; escape output in any HTML surfaces.
- Rate-limit auth/OTP/public payment init.
- CSRF: cookie-based browser flows need same-site / CSRF strategy; mobile bearer APIs rely on token + TLS.

## Android

- Prefer encrypted prefs for tokens (`SecurePreferences`).
- Do not log auth tokens, OTP codes, or HMAC secrets.
- Root / lock screens exist for a reason — do not weaken them casually.

## AI / agent

- Never write exploit PoCs against production.
- Never paste production secrets into docs or chat logs.
- Do not disable TLS verification.
